course: dictionary
lesson: 12536
title: Detached: one word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. Ask yourself what is being described: a house, a thing, or a person. That clue shows the meaning. «Our house is detached, so no wall joins it to the house next door.» A house is the subject here, so detached must mean standing on its own.
explain: «Mum detached the tear-off slip from the bottom of the form.» Something was separated from something else. Swap in your meaning, "Mum separated the slip from the form", and check it still makes sense. It does, so you have the right meaning.
explain: People can be detached too. «Sam sat at the back of the room, detached and silent, as if the game had nothing to do with him.» Detached here describes how Sam feels: he is not involved and does not show much emotion. The clue is "as if the game had nothing to do with him."
fact: Detached means separated or taken off from something.
fact: A detached house stands on its own and is not joined to another house.
fact: Semi-detached houses are joined on one side, and terraced houses are in a row.
fact: A detached person seems not involved, cold or far away, and does not show much emotion.
fact: In science, a detached retina is a serious eye problem where the back layer of the eye comes away.
exercise: «Our house is detached, so no wall joins it to the house next door.» What does detached mean here? | Joined to another house | Painted in lots of colours | Very tall and thin | *Standing on its own
exercise: «Mum detached the tear-off slip from the bottom of the form.» What does detached mean here? | Lost in the post | *Separated or taken off | Stuck together | Glued back on
exercise: «Sam sat at the back, detached and silent, as if the game had nothing to do with him.» What does detached suggest about Sam? | Very excited and loud | Hungry and tired | *Not involved or showing much feeling | Cold because it is winter
test: «The semi-detached house had a wall shared with its neighbour.» What does detached mean in this sentence? | Painted bright blue | Joined to every house in the street | Very large and grand | *Not fully joined, standing apart on one side
test: «Ella seemed detached from the argument and did not take sides.» What does detached mean here? | Stuck fast to the group | Carried away by the wind | Angry and shouting | *Not involved or emotionally distant
exam: Mo reads «The rope had detached from the boat.» Which meaning fits best, and why? | It was painted in the boat's colours, because detached means painted | It was happy to be on the boat, because detached means happy | *It came loose and separated from the boat, because the rope is no longer joined to it | It was very long, because detached means long
